    SORENSEN'S OFFICE (S5 §3.8). The keypad takes a code nobody has
    (password, so the PIN cracker can't skip it, S4 P11); HaX opens it on the
    deck choice. The safe: PIN 060216 (Kowalczyk's cracker, or the rent
    ledger's header read the long way). PLACEHOLDER map: room_hce_office. %>
    "sorensen_office": {
      "type": "room_hce_office",
      "door_sign": "Director -- M. Sorensen",
      "locked": true,
      "lockType": "password",
      "requires": "<%= office_code %>",
      "connections": {
        "east": "restricted_stacks"
      },
      "objects": [
        {
          "type": "safe",
          "sprite": "safe1",
          "id": "director_safe",
          "name": "Floor Safe",
          "position": { "x": 6.5, "y": 7.5 },
          "takeable": false,
          "locked": true,
          "lockType": "pin",
          "requires": "<%= safe_pin %>",
          "pinLength": 6,
          "observations": "A floor safe with a six-digit keypad.",
          "puzzle_graph_role": "container",
          "puzzle_graph_unlocks": "tape_room",
          "puzzle_graph_note": "Holds the tape room key card (and the Reading, the master schedule).",
          "contents": [
            {
              "type": "notes",
              "id": "the_reading",
              "name": "The Reading, 1: Viral Dynamics",
              "takeable": true,
              "readable": true,
              "observations": "A thin file in a sloping hand. The first page is about you.",
              "text": "<%= reading_head %>Lawson was arrested and kept his promise to me. Their file does not say who arrested him.",
              "textVariants": [
                { "condition": "globalVars.m01_final_choice === 'fight'", "value": "<%= reading_head %>They put Lawson on the floor when the argument was already won. Force first. Noted." },
                { "condition": "globalVars.m01_final_choice === 'arrest'", "value": "<%= reading_head %>They read Lawson his rights. He kept his promise to me and said nothing." },
                { "condition": "globalVars.m01_final_choice === '' && globalVars.m01_completed", "value": "<%= reading_head %>They read Lawson his rights. He kept his promise to me and said nothing." },
                { "condition": "globalVars.m01_final_choice === 'recruit'", "value": "<%= reading_head %>They offered Lawson a deal. A recruiter's instinct. They should be careful whom they show it to." },
                { "condition": "globalVars.m01_final_choice === 'expose'", "value": "<%= reading_head %>They gave Lawson's figures to the press. Applications rose. I keep the figure." },
                { "condition": "globalVars.m01_final_choice === 'surrender'", "value": "<%= reading_head %>Lawson put the device down when they asked. It is the only order of mine he enjoyed." }
              ],
              "onPickup": { "setVariable": { "reading_found": true } },
              "puzzle_graph_role": "evidence"
            },
            {
              "type": "notes",
              "id": "the_reading_2",
              "name": "The Reading, 2: The Innocents",
              "takeable": true,
              "readable": true,
              "observations": "The second page of the file, in the same hand.",
              "text": "THE INNOCENTS\nTheir first days are not in my file. Someone at SAFETYNET is careful with them.",
              "textVariants": [
                { "condition": "globalVars.m02_patient_assaulted", "value": "THE INNOCENTS\nThey struck a patient on a ward. I have read the ward's notes. So, I expect, have they." },
                { "condition": "globalVars.m01_completed && globalVars.m01_kevin_ko", "value": "THE INNOCENTS\nOn their first day they put a bystander on the floor. They will have told themselves it was necessary." },
                { "condition": "globalVars.m01_completed && globalVars.m01_sarah_ko", "value": "THE INNOCENTS\nOn their first day they put a bystander on the floor. They will have told themselves it was necessary." },
                { "condition": "globalVars.m01_completed && globalVars.m01_maya_ko", "value": "THE INNOCENTS\nOn their first day they put a bystander on the floor. They will have told themselves it was necessary." },
                { "condition": "globalVars.m01_completed", "value": "THE INNOCENTS\nNot one bystander hurt on their first day. Rare. It will not last." }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "notes",
              "id": "the_reading_3",
              "name": "The Reading, 3: Albion",
              "takeable": true,
              "readable": true,
              "observations": "The third page of the file, in the same hand.",
              "text": "ALBION\nTheir report went upstairs and no further. I will not guess what it said.",
              "textVariants": [
                { "condition": "globalVars.m04_disclosure_choice === 'full'", "value": "ALBION\nThey told the inquiry everything, and every site was audited. My lesson, delivered by them. They do not know it yet." },
                { "condition": "globalVars.m04_disclosure_choice === 'partial'", "value": "ALBION\nThey told half. Half is how we arrived here." },
                { "condition": "globalVars.m04_disclosure_choice === 'quiet'", "value": "ALBION\nThey buried it. They understand me better than they admit." }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "notes",
              "id": "the_reading_4",
              "name": "The Reading, 4: Portland",
              "takeable": true,
              "readable": true,
              "observations": "The fourth page of the file, in the same hand.",
              "text": "PORTLAND\nOne team, four sites. They sent it where they were told. Obedience or trust. I will learn which.",
              "textVariants": [
                { "condition": "globalVars.m07_debrief_stance === 'defended'", "value": "PORTLAND\n'I'd make it again.' They would. I have counted on it." },
                { "condition": "globalVars.m07_debrief_stance === 'owned'", "value": "PORTLAND\nThey said it was theirs. They will carry this too." },
                { "condition": "globalVars.m07_debrief_stance === 'refused'", "value": "PORTLAND\n'Don't ask me to rank them.' I ranked them for them." },
                { "condition": "globalVars.m07_debrief_stance === 'hardened'", "value": "PORTLAND\nThey asked for the numbers. Good. I keep numbers." }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "notes",
              "id": "the_reading_last_page",
              "name": "The Reading, Last Page",
              "takeable": true,
              "readable": true,
              "observations": "The last page. A pencilled line in the margin, older than the ink.",
              "text": "When the hour comes, they will be in the room and the key will be in reach. They will press it. I will not need to ask. They will have read this far and found nothing here that is untrue.\nBelow: Their handler will cover for them. She was taught to.\nPencilled in the margin: They will save Lawson's file. They will want to know why he did it.",
              "onRead": { "setVariable": { "reading_finished": true } }
            },
            {
              "type": "notes",
              "id": "master_schedule",
              "name": "Destruction Schedule (master)",
              "takeable": true,
              "readable": true,
              "observations": "The order's schedule, ticked room by room in pencil.",
              "text": "Series by number, per the order. -- A.\nIn pencil, room by room: Dock ✓. Front desk ✓. Reading room ✓. Open stacks ✓. Closet ✓. Stacks ✓. Cage ✓. Office ✓. Tape room ✓. Salvage cage, no series, no tick.\nIn the margin: Reading (safe). Plan chest: not listed. Keep?",
              "onRead": { "setVariable": { "schedule_read": true } }
            },
            {
              "type": "keycard",
              "id": "tape_room_keycard",
              "name": "Key Card, Tape Store",
              "takeable": true,
              "card_id": "tape_room_reader",
              "opens_lock": "tape_room_reader",
              "observations": "A key card on a lanyard. The tag says TAPE STORE.",
              "puzzle_graph_role": "key",
              "puzzle_graph_unlocks": "tape_room"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_comment": "S6 §1.7. Read in place; its header is the safe's PIN the long way. rent_ledger_read latches HaX's Irina line (A3-24).",
          "type": "notes",
          "sprite": "book1",
          "id": "rent_book",
          "name": "Rent Ledger",
