          "text": "PRINTER READY. TRAY EMPTY.",
          "textVariants": [
            { "condition": "globalVars.flag3_submitted", "value": "CATALOGUE ENTRY -- VULNERABILITY HOLDINGS\nRef: VH-2017-0312. Authentication bypass, Carrow Controls RM-4 remote-management module.\nDeployed at: grid battery sites, water treatment works, substations. Approx. 400 UK sites.\nVendor aware: no.\nDisposition: RETAIN. Operational value. Review 2019.\nBoard: OPS ✓ LEGAL ✓ TECH ✓ INT ✓ STRAT ......\n\nMEMO. To: Disposition Board. From: Chief Strategist. 14 March 2017. Re: VH-2017-0312.\nWe are holding a flaw in a Carrow controller because it may one day be useful to us. It will certainly one day be useful to someone else.\nFour hundred sites run this module. Their engineers cannot patch what nobody has told them about, and we cannot defend them from it, having chosen not to.\nI recommend notification to the vendor within thirty days. I have drafted the notice. I would rather send it than explain later why we didn't.\nA. Tesseract\n\nDRAFT, NOT SENT. 14 March 2017. To: Product Security, Carrow Controls. Re: RM-4 remote-management module.\nWe have found a flaw in the RM-4 module that lets an unauthenticated user on the management network issue control commands. A test case is attached for your engineers.\nWe will keep this confidential for ninety days from the date of this letter, or until a fix ships, whichever is sooner, so that your customers have time to patch. We are glad to help with testing.\nWith thanks,\nDr Adrian Tesseract, Chief Strategist" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "notes",
          "sprite": "notes1",
          "id": "mirror_job_printout",
          "name": "Mirror Job Printout",
          "position": { "x": 7.4, "y": 3.5 },
          "takeable": false,
          "readable": true,
          "observations": "Printer tray, empty.",
          "observationVariants": [
            { "condition": "globalVars.flag4_submitted", "value": "Two pages in the printer tray. The first is signed." }
          ],
          "text": "PRINTER READY. TRAY EMPTY.",
          "textVariants": [
            { "condition": "globalVars.flag4_submitted", "value": "PROJECTED DEATHS ATTRIBUTABLE TO THE PUBLICATION, FIRST THIRTY DAYS\nRelease by key, all cities: 1,100 to 2,600.\nFallback by city: fewer, later.\nPrincipal causes: hospital systems (dispatch, infusion, records); grid control; water treatment.\nAssumes the cells move first.\nAn acceptable price for the last arms race. -- A.\n\nRELEASE CONFIGURATION\nManual, at console. Single key. Requires an operator present.\nFallback: 06:00 UTC, staged by city." }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_comment": "S5 §3.10: the enrolment binders in a picked crate (optional). Lockpick only by design: no key exists, so the validator's 'nothing can open it' warning is expected.",
